# Scope of this license

This MIT license covers the **source code** in this repository:

- `src/main/java/com/wdcdp/**` — the CDP backend, original work
- `src/main/java/de/keksuccino/rinku/**` — a compatibility layer, original work
- build scripts, documentation and tooling in this repository

## What it does not cover

### `releases/webdisplays-1.2.25-26.1.2.jar`

This jar contains code derived from **WebDisplays by montoyo**, which its author
released into the **public domain**:

> This mod and its source code is now in public domain. Feel free to do whatever
> you want with it; make forks, distribute it... whatever. I would appreciate it,
> of course, if you credited me.

It is redistributed here under those terms. It is **not** covered by the MIT
license above, and credit belongs to montoyo. The 26.1.2 port in this jar was
made for this project.

### The package name `de.keksuccino.rinku`

The package name is kept so that WebDisplays' reflective method lookup succeeds —
it resolves `de.keksuccino.rinku.Rinku` and its two listener interfaces by exact
binary name.

**The code inside it is an independent implementation, not a copy of the
original Rinku.** No source from Keksuccino's Rinku is included here. The name is
used only for binary compatibility, which package names permit.

## Third-party dependencies

This project compiles against, but does not redistribute, NeoForge, Minecraft and
LWJGL. Each is governed by its own license. `cp.example.txt` lists the jars you
need; obtain them from their official sources.

## Attribution

- **montoyo** — author of WebDisplays (public domain)
- **Keksuccino** — author of the original Rinku, whose API surface this project
  matches for compatibility
